---
/**
 * The caveat that closes a section, set below a rule and in the UI face.
 *
 * Every act that makes a claim ends with the thing that claim does not cover.
 * Giving that its own component is what keeps it from being optional.
 *
 * It is a <div> rather than a <p> because the text inside is Markdown, and
 * Markdown emits its own paragraphs. A <p> wrapping a <p> is invalid, and a
 * browser resolves it by closing the outer one early -- which silently strips
 * the note styling from the very text it was meant to mark. The div also lets
 * a note run to two paragraphs, which the old markup could not.
 */
import s from "../../sections/Section.module.css";
---

<div class={s.note}><slot /></div>
